WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.510
Netflix is heating up this June with an exciting
slate of new releases.

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:09.470
From new seasons of fan favorites to pulse-pounding
original films, here are the best new Netflix

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:12.560
releases to add to your queue in June 2019.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:17.500
We're kicking off the month with one of the
most hotly anticipated returns of the year.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:22.260
Black Mirror is storming onto Netflix, and
the episode lineup looks just as crazy as

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.580
the past installments.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:28.460
Thanks to a series of trailers for the upcoming
fifth season, we have an idea of what each

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.260
of the three new episodes will entail.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:35.160
In "Rachel, Jack and Ashley too," a lonely
girl finally gets the chance to meet her favorite

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:40.660
singer via a toy called an "Ashley Too," only
things get dark when the toy appears to channel

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:43.220
more than the pop star's personality.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:47.760
In "Striking Vipers," a chance encounter kicks
off a string of events that soon spiral out

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:48.600
of control.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:53.220
And in "Smithereens," an unbalanced cab driver
goes on the ride of his life.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:55.340
The whole season drops on June 5th.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:01:00.720
The early days of Netflix originals were filled
with now-iconic titles, but one show stood

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:06.130
out prominently enough to reach cult classic
status: 3%, the Brazilian dystopian thriller

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:08.880
you never knew you were missing until you
watched it.

00:01:09.229 --> 00:01:13.760
The first season of 3% introduced the premise
of a population of young adults who have to

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:17.980
compete against each other in a cutthroat
competition called The Process.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:22.180
Only three percent of participants make it
through and get the chance to live beyond

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:23.180
famine and poverty.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:28.280
We can't get into the details of the rest
of the season or its follow-up without spoiling

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:33.340
all the twists, so suffice it to say that
3% is binge TV at its finest.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.180
Check it out when the third season drops on
June 7th.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:41.360
Cooking and travel shows are a dime a dozen,
but Netflix's upcoming original The Chef Show

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:44.420
deserves a special mention, mainly for the
people involved.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:50.240
The series sees Iron Man director Jon Favreau
stepping in as producer, director, and star,

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:51.990
alongside chef Roy Choi.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:56.480
It's basically Jon Favreau cooking things
and talking about food, which is fine all

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:01.020
by itself, but the trailer also showcases
some instantly familiar faces.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:06.840
Yup, it looks like half the stars of the MCU
stopped by, with Robert Downey, Jr., Tom Holland,

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:11.180
Gwyneth Paltrow, and even Kevin Feige and
the Russo brothers sit down for a meal.

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:15.680
If Jon Favreau in an apron looks familiar,
that's because the concept for the show came

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:20.480
out of his own 2014 film Chef, for which Roy
Choi taught him how to cook.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:21.980
As Favreau explained:

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:26.400
"During the production of Chef, I developed
a much deeper understanding of the ways in

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.940
which we express our emotions, share our cultures,
and seek meaningful connections through the

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:32.280
act of cooking and eating."

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:36.840
The kitchen is my domain, that was our deal
… I don't give a f--- what the deal was."

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:40.920
If that sounds like something in your wheelhouse,
be sure to tune in on June 7th when The Chef

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:42.080
Show starts cooking.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:47.260
Netflix has been killing it with their original
sci-fi thrillers, and now I Am Mother is set

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:48.360
to continue that trend.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:54.000
Starring Oscar-winner Hilary Swank and young
actress Clara Rugaard, I Am Mother is set

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.540
in the future and follows a young girl who's
raised by a robot named Mother in an underground

00:02:58.540 --> 00:02:59.040
vault.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:03.000
From birth, she's taught that the outside
world is an uninhabitable wasteland.

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:07.300
But the appearance of a woman from the outside
throws that narrative into question.

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:12.360
In an exclusive interview, director Grant
Sputore explained that while the film explores

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:16.989
our relationship with the high-tech future
we're creating, the thematic elements go even

00:03:16.989 --> 00:03:17.480
deeper.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.220
"For me, what it's really about is the discussion
of what it means to be a good person.

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:26.260
How do you work out right from wrong, how
do you work out who you are, separate to what

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:27.620
your parents want you to be?"

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:32.280
Basically, get ready for a mind-bending adventure
when I Am Mother premieres on June 7.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:37.760
Music lovers will get a trip down memory lane
on June 12th with Rolling Thunder Revue: A

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:40.040
Bob Dylan Story by Martin Scorsese.

00:03:40.469 --> 00:03:45.080
With this upcoming documentary, the acclaimed
filmmaker is taking viewers on a musical odyssey

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:49.220
into The Rolling Thunder Revue tour, which
saw Dylan crossing the country to play in

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:54.040
smaller, more intimate venues in an attempt
to get back to his roots -- and his fans.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:57.680
And with Martin Scorsese at the helm, there's
no telling what to expect.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:02.160
Bob Dylan may be the perfect subject for a
filmmaker who loves to put a little crazy

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:02.760
in his films.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:16.020
Turn it up when Rolling Thunder Revue: A Bob
Dylan Story drops on June 12th.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:21.100
Adam Sandler's films are a little like a blind
gunman shooting at a running horse.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:24.880
There are plenty of misses, but every now
and then one of those bullets is bound to

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:25.480
hit meat.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:28.740
Murder Mystery looks like it just might be
a bullseye.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:33.320
Co-starring Jennifer Aniston, Murder Mystery
follows a New York couple who take a second

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:37.900
honeymoon to Europe and get embroiled in the
murder of a billionaire on his private yacht.

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:42.780
Soon, they're the prime suspects in the crime,
and they have to go on a hilarious, action-packed

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:46.920
quest to prove their innocence...and maybe
find the true murderer in the process.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:48.200
Buckle up for the ride.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.360
Murder Mystery premieres on June 14th.

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:55.380
Anthony Anderson headlines Beats as a former
music producer who's gone through some rough

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:59.160
times and has ended up working as a security
guard at a Chicago school.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:04.500
There, he meets a troubled young student with
a gift for music, and together the two may

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.660
just find a way to triumph over their pasts.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:11.160
Beats looks like a heartwarming, inspirational
drama that won't pull any punches.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:13.560
Take a look when Beats arrives on June 19th.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:19.160
True crime is apparently a big hit for Netflix,
and that's a win-win for fans of the genre,

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:24.100
too, because there's no shortage of true crime
docs to binge on the streaming service.

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:29.690
On top of explosive hits like Making a Murderer,
Netflix recently introduced The Confession

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:34.380
Tapes, which as of Season 1 is sitting with
a 100% rating on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:38.900
The show focuses on confessed criminals who
later claimed that they'd been coerced into

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:40.180
giving their confessions.

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:44.920
This show takes a deep dive into the shocking
crimes and explores how the original confessions

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:46.520
may have changed everything.

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:51.960
Season 2 arrives on June 21st, perfectly timed
for an early binge to kick off the summer.

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:57.040
If you like dark dramas that have a tendency
to blow your mind, you'll love Dark.

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:02.440
Part thriller, part sci-fi, and part supernatural,
Dark follows three separate generations as

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:04.480
they all work to find missing children.

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:09.740
The first season of this German series premiered
on Netflix to rave reviews, yet still remains

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:12.060
something of a hidden gem on the streaming
service.

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:16.560
If you haven't caught the first season yet,
do yourself a favor and add it to your queue.

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:21.310
You can watch it in its original German with
subtitles, or the English dubbed version if

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:23.720
you prefer, but definitely give it a shot
either way.

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:28.480
Now that Season 2 is on its way on June 21st,
there's never been a better time to discover

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:30.160
this fantastic series.

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:35.960
For two seasons, Netflix's documentary series
Dope has offered an unprecedented street-level

00:06:35.970 --> 00:06:40.830
look into the American drug war, focusing
on the lives and crimes of the people on both

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:42.680
sides of the ongoing conflict.

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:47.760
From task forces raiding homes and production
facilities to the dangers smugglers face on

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:52.640
a day-to-day basis, Dope have given viewers
an uncompromising glimpse into what it's really

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:55.360
like in this dangerously topsy turvy world.

00:06:55.780 --> 00:07:00.620
Drugs, guns, and cash are set to take center
stage for a third season of the highly rated

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:03.480
docuseries, which premieres on June 28th.

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:08.280
Even though all of Netflix's Marvel shows
have officially been canned, there's still

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:10.500
one final season to look forward to.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:15.220
Marvel's Jessica Jones has followed the titular
heroine through a whirlwind two seasons that

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:19.800
saw her taking on the villainous puppetmaster
Kilgrave and then kind of taking on her best

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:20.700
friend Trish.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.860
Where will Season 3 take us?

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:27.740
Netflix so far hasn't given a solid release
date for the third season of Jessica Jones,

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:29.660
so keep your eyes peeled for it to show up.

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:33.320
Those are all the Netflix originals we're
getting excited about.

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:37.660
Now here are the rest of the hot new titles
coming to Netflix in June 2019.

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:42.460
Curiously enough, Netflix's best new action
releases are all animated.

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:47.100
Sure, we've got Batman Begins and The Dark
Knight joining the service in June, but those

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:49.280
films seem to come and go pretty often.

00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:53.840
More exciting, of course, is the addition
of Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse, which

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:57.840
is nothing short of a 117-minute hurricane
of pure fun.

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:01.420
"Act super normal, selecting a bagel … Spiderman?

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:03.640
… You know that's funny, I get that a lot."

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:09.380
That's dropping later in the month, on June
26th, and just a bit earlier, on June 21st,

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:15.400
comes another surprise the entire run of Neon
Genesis Evangelion and two full-length Evangelion

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:15.900
films

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:17.360
Interested in thrills?

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:22.120
On June 1st, look for Carrie...although since
there's no date attached, it's unclear if

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:26.720
it's going to be the original 1976 version
or the 2013 remake.

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:28.820
Just gonna have to roll the dice on this one.

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:32.860
“Don't be in such a hurry...I'm hurrinhawaeffumyou,
ya know that?"

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:38.680
On June 16th, look for Cop Car, a silly sounding
film that's actually a suspenseful, well-made

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:43.740
low-budget thriller starring Kevin Bacon as
a no-good cop hunting down two kids who steal

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:44.320
his car.

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:47.040
“Ha.”

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:54.620
There's a big load of drama dropping on June
1st, including a few classics that never get

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:55.120
old.

00:08:55.380 --> 00:09:00.860
Keep your eyes peeled for Platoon, as well
as Network, a 1976 satire about the news media

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:03.220
industry that pulled in four Oscar wins.

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:04.020
What else?

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:09.640
50/50 is an understated dramedy starring Seth
Rogen and Joseph Gordon-Levitt, and The Space

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:14.030
Between Us stars Asa Butterfield as a boy
on Mars who comes back to Earth and learns

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:15.020
about being human.

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:19.800
Finally, Gran Torino is also popping in on
the first to remind you to stay off Clint

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:20.800
Eastwood's lawn.

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:22.960
"Get off my lawn."

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:27.640
We're also looking at a smattering of new
TV seasons crossing into the Netflix jungle

00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:28.140
in June.

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:31.600
On the first of the month, check out the second
season of Dynasty.

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:36.260
On the 3rd, you can binge Documentary Now!:
Season 3, which is bringing in a whole new

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:39.800
cast of guest stars for its ridiculous mockumentary
narratives.

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:44.200
Finally, keep your eyes peeled for Season
3 of Shooter on the 21st.

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:46.700
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:50.820
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
shows are coming soon.

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:54.160
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

